+# ArbiLend — Security Audit Report
+
+**Scope:** `src/LendingMarket.sol`, `src/CollateralVault.sol`, `src/PriceOracle.sol`,
+`src/MarketProxy.sol`, `src/interfaces/*` @ commit `e2934f0`.
+**Target chain:** Arbitrum One. **Status:** pre-deployment, no test suite.
+**Review type:** manual, full-coverage. Report only — no source files were modified.
+
+---
+
+## Verdict
+
+**Do not deploy.** Seven issues are individually sufficient for an attacker to take the
+entire market. Three of them (C-1, C-2, C-3) are unprotected privileged setters that
+require no capital, no timing and no special position — a bot scanning newly-verified
+Arbitrum contracts would find them within minutes of deployment. Two more (C-5, C-6)
+mean the market misprices and wrongly liquidates honest users *even if nobody attacks it*.
+
+The list is ranked. Everything down to and including **H-5** should be fixed before any
+real USDC touches this. Below that, the Mediums are the difference between "safe launch"
+and "safe launch that survives the weETH/ezETH/USDT listings on the roadmap".
+
+---
+
+## Ranked summary
+
+| # | Severity | Contract · Function | Issue |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| C-1 | Critical | `LendingMarket.upgradeTo` | No access control — anyone can replace the implementation |
+| C-2 | Critical | `LendingMarket.setOracle` | No access control — anyone can install a fake price source |
+| C-3 | Critical | `LendingMarket.setLiquidationThreshold` | No access control — anyone can disable solvency checks |
+| C-4 | Critical | `CollateralVault.withdraw` | Transfer before state write + stale cached balance → vault drain |
+| C-5 | Critical | `LendingMarket.healthFactor` | Division before multiplication → honest users liquidated at 2× collateral |
+| C-6 | Critical | `PriceOracle.getPrice` | `latestAnswer()` with no staleness, round or sign validation |
+| C-7 | Critical | `LendingMarket.borrowWithSig` | No nonce, no deadline → infinite signature replay |
