+
+## C-4 — `CollateralVault.withdraw` transfers before writing state, and writes a stale balance
+
+**Contract · function:** `CollateralVault.withdraw` (`src/CollateralVault.sol:44`)
+
+```solidity
+uint256 balance = balanceOf[msg.sender][token];
+if (balance < amount) revert InsufficientBalance();
+
+IERC20(token).transfer(msg.sender, amount);          // external call
+balanceOf[msg.sender][token] = balance - amount;     // written from a CACHED read
+ILendingMarket(market).requireHealthy(msg.sender);
+```
+
+Two compounding defects. The token transfer happens **before** the balance is decremented,
+and the decrement is computed from `balance`, cached *before* the external call — so any
+nested update is not just racy, it is silently overwritten. Compare `seize` on line 55,
+which decrements first and gets the ordering right.
+
+**What the attacker gets:** the vault, if any listed collateral can call back into the caller
+during `transfer`. Deposit 100. Call `withdraw(50)`. In the token's transfer hook, re-enter
+`withdraw(50)`: the inner call re-reads `balance == 100`, passes the check, transfers another
+50, writes `balanceOf = 50`, and `requireHealthy` passes because the user has no debt. The
+outer frame then writes `balanceOf = balance - amount = 100 - 50 = 50` — clobbering the inner
+write. The user received 100 tokens and the vault still credits them 50. Repeat until the
+vault is empty; the tokens drained belong to other depositors.
+
+wstETH itself has no transfer hook, so this is not exploitable on day one with the launch
+config alone. But the README states the DAO has asked for "a path to yield-bearing and
+rebasing collateral," and this is exactly the class of token that ships with hooks (ERC-777,
+ERC-1363, and most LRT wrappers with custom transfer logic). This is a loaded gun pointed at
+the collateral listing roadmap, and it is one line of reordering to defuse.
+
+**Fix:** apply checks-effects-interactions and stop using the cached value:
+
+```solidity
+uint256 balance = balanceOf[msg.sender][token];
+if (balance < amount) revert InsufficientBalance();
+balanceOf[msg.sender][token] = balance - amount;     // effect first
+ILendingMarket(market).requireHealthy(msg.sender);   // solvency check on final state
+IERC20(token).safeTransfer(msg.sender, amount);      // interaction last
+```
+
+Also add a `nonReentrant` guard to `deposit`, `withdraw` and `seize` as defence in depth —
+`_liquidate` calls `vault.seize` in a loop and hands tokens to `msg.sender` mid-loop, which
+is a second re-entry surface into the same accounting.
+
