+
+## C-6 — `PriceOracle.getPrice` performs no validation on the Chainlink answer
+
+**Contract · function:** `PriceOracle.getPrice` (`src/PriceOracle.sol:39`)
+
+```solidity
+int256 answer = feed.latestAnswer();
+return uint256(answer) * 10 ** (18 - feed.decimals());
+```
+
+`latestAnswer()` is the deprecated V2 accessor. It returns a bare integer with **no
+`updatedAt` timestamp and no `roundId`**, so the contract has structurally no way to tell a
+price from one second ago apart from one from three weeks ago. There is also no check that
+`answer > 0`.
+
+**What the attacker gets, and what the unlucky user gets:**
+- *Stale price.* If the wstETH aggregator stops updating — feed deprecation, an OCR node-set
+  failure, or Chainlink retiring the feed after the wstETH/USD feed supersedes it — the
+  market keeps quoting the last value forever. The moment the real price diverges, whichever
+  side is favourable gets arbitraged: borrow against collateral that is really worth less, or
+  liquidate positions that are really solvent. The market carries the entire loss.
+- *Negative answer.* `uint256(answer)` on a negative `int256` wraps to a number near `2^256`.
+  A single negative print on any collateral feed makes `collateralValueUsd` astronomically
+  large for anyone holding one wei of that token, and the market's whole USDC balance is
+  borrowable in the same block. USD feeds rarely go negative, but this is a one-line check
+  standing between you and total loss, and the roadmap adds more feeds.
+
+**Fix:** use `latestRoundData` and validate all of it:
+
+```solidity
+(uint80 roundId, int256 answer,, uint256 updatedAt, uint80 answeredInRound) = feed.latestRoundData();
+if (answer <= 0) revert InvalidPrice(token);
+if (updatedAt == 0 || answeredInRound < roundId) revert IncompleteRound(token);
+if (block.timestamp - updatedAt > heartbeat[token]) revert StalePrice(token);
+```
+
+Store a per-token `heartbeat` alongside the feed (Chainlink publishes each feed's heartbeat
+and deviation threshold; set yours to heartbeat + a small buffer, not a single global
+constant — the shortlisted feeds have different heartbeats). Set it in `setFeed` so a feed
+can never be listed without one.
+
