+
+## C-7 — `borrowWithSig` signatures are replayable forever
+
+**Contract · function:** `LendingMarket.borrowWithSig` (`src/LendingMarket.sol:162`)
+
+```solidity
+bytes32 structHash = keccak256(abi.encode(BORROW_TYPEHASH, borrower, amount));
+bytes32 digest = keccak256(abi.encodePacked("\x19\x01", domainSeparator, structHash));
+if (ecrecover(digest, v, r, s) != borrower) revert BadSignature();
+_borrow(borrower, amount);
+```
+
+The signed struct is `Borrow(address borrower,uint256 amount)` — **no nonce and no
+deadline**. Nothing is consumed or invalidated when the signature is used. The same
+`(v, r, s)` is valid on every call, forever.
+
+**What the attacker gets:** a borrower signs once to delegate a 1,000 USDC borrow. Anyone
+who observes that signature — it is public in calldata the moment it is first used — replays
+it repeatedly. Each replay adds another 1,000 USDC of debt to the signer's position and
+pushes the USDC to the signer, so the attacker is not stealing the loan proceeds directly.
+They are doing something more profitable: driving the victim's health factor down until the
+position is liquidatable, then calling `liquidate(victim)` and taking the victim's entire
+collateral at a 5% bonus. The replay loop terminates on its own at exactly the point where
+the attacker's payday begins — `_borrow` reverts when `healthFactor < WAD`, i.e. one replay
+after the position becomes seizable.
+
+It also drains market liquidity on demand and, combined with H-3, lets an attacker cheaply
+grow the `borrowers` array.
+
+**Fix:** add a per-signer nonce and a deadline to the typehash and check both:
+
+```solidity
+bytes32 internal constant BORROW_TYPEHASH =
+    keccak256("Borrow(address borrower,uint256 amount,uint256 nonce,uint256 deadline)");
+...
+if (block.timestamp > deadline) revert SignatureExpired();
+bytes32 structHash = keccak256(abi.encode(BORROW_TYPEHASH, borrower, amount, nonces[borrower]++, deadline));
+```
+
+Use OpenZeppelin's `ECDSA.recover` rather than raw `ecrecover` — it rejects `address(0)` and
+the malleable upper-half `s` values for you (see L-2). Note that the storage layout is
+append-only per the README, so `mapping(address => uint256) nonces` must be appended after
+`domainSeparator`.
+
