+# Low / informational
+
+- **L-1 — Cached `domainSeparator`.** `src/LendingMarket.sol:71`. `block.chainid` is baked in at
+  initialization. If Arbitrum One ever forks, signatures are valid on both chains. Recompute the
+  separator when `block.chainid` differs from the cached value (the standard OZ `EIP712`
+  pattern).
+
+- **L-2 — Raw `ecrecover`.** `src/LendingMarket.sol:165`. Returns `address(0)` for malformed
+  signatures — harmless only because `borrower` is never `address(0)` in practice — and accepts
+  malleable upper-half `s` values, so one authorisation has two valid encodings. Currently moot
+  because C-7 makes replay unlimited anyway, but it must be fixed *with* C-7 or the nonce can be
+  bypassed. Use `ECDSA.recover`.
+
+- **L-3 — Dust principal survives full repayment.** `src/LendingMarket.sol:178`.
+  `amount * WAD / borrowIndex` floors, so repaying the exact `debtOf` leaves a wei or two of
+  principal. The position never truly closes, keeps accruing, and the borrower stays in the
+  `borrowers` array (H-3). Add a `repayAll()` that zeroes `principalOf` directly, or snap to zero
+  when the residual falls below a dust threshold.
+
+- **L-4 — ETH trapped in the proxy.** `src/MarketProxy.sol:38`. `receive()` is payable and the
+  fallback is payable, but `LendingMarket` has no ETH handling and no sweep. Any ETH sent to the
+  market is permanently lost. Remove `receive()` unless there is a reason for it.
+
+- **L-5 — Missing input validation.** `borrow`/`_borrow` accept `amount == 0` (see H-3);
+  `initialize` does not reject zero addresses for `owner_`, `oracle_`, `vault_` or `debtAsset_`;
+  `PriceOracle.setFeed` does not reject the zero feed. Also, the `NotCollateral` error is
+  declared on `src/LendingMarket.sol:35` and never used — a hint that a collateral check was
+  intended somewhere and did not land.
+
+- **L-6 — No liquidator slippage bound.** `liquidate(address)` takes no maximum repayment. Between
+  transaction submission and execution, `accrueInterest` can raise the debt, so the liquidator
+  pays more than they quoted. Add a `maxDebtRepaid` parameter.
+
+- **L-7 — No tests.** The README acknowledges this. Independently of everything above, the fixes
+  for C-5, C-7, H-3 and H-5 all touch subtle arithmetic and are not safely verifiable by
+  inspection. Before deploying, the suite needs at minimum: health-factor boundary tests across
+  the full LTV range (which would have caught C-5 immediately), interest-accrual tests across
+  long idle periods, signature-replay tests, liquidation tests for the deeply-underwater case,
+  and a fork test against real Arbitrum feed addresses to catch H-2 and M-4.
+
